      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Cumulative spend by dispatch origin",
      "description": "The relay-vs-interactive split. Relay workers carry catalyst_orchestration=\"relay\"; an interactive session sets nothing, so unattributed burn shows in the second series. Lines are CUMULATIVE per bucket (see below), not a rate. \u26a0\ufe0f Aggregated with `max_over_time`, NOT `increase`. These are per-session cumulative counters that expire 15m after their last sample, so a short relay phase can expose only its first nonzero sample and `increase()` would treat that as the baseline and report ~0. `max_over_time` takes each session series' final value; summing across sessions gives the true total. Same pattern as operator-usage.json.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
